    position_id: "310e8cab-e76b-42cf-9256-ee101e1177a5",
    title: "Office Help",
    jd_reference: "BVT/HR/JD/2026/039",
    summary: "Keep the BlynkEx office clean, hygienic and tidy every day: floors, meeting rooms, the pantry and washrooms. You work around desks, screens and papers, so you never read, move or throw away anything on a desk, and you hand anything you find to the HR Manager.",
    description: "As an Office Help you look after the cleanliness and hygiene of our office. You work 8 hours a day, as per the roster.\n\nYou work around desks, screens and papers all day, but never read, move, photograph or throw away anything on them.\n\nWhat you'll do\n• Clean floors, common areas, meeting rooms, the pantry and washrooms daily, and again when needed\n• Keep washrooms clean and stocked with soap, tissue and sanitiser, and tell the HR Manager before cleaning materials run out\n• Wipe only the clear parts of a desk; never move papers, devices or personal things\n• Wash pantry utensils, clean appliances after use and keep the drinking water area clean\n• Collect and separate waste every day, and dispose of it the approved way\n• Leave paper on desks and printers alone; staff put it in the shred bin\n• Keep fire exits, corridors and emergency equipment clear\n• Hand any document, device, key card or other item you find to the HR Manager, without reading it\n• Report damage, leaks, electrical faults, pests or safety risks to the HR Manager the same day\n\nWho you'll work with\nYou report to the HR Manager, as part of our support staff. You work with the Office Assistant on the pantry and meeting rooms, and send visitors to the Security Guard or reception.",
    requirements: "• Able to read Hindi well enough to follow the cleaning schedule and safety labels\n• Physically fit for cleaning work across the whole office\n• Willing to work 8-hour rostered shifts across the office's operating hours\n• Honest and on time, and able to keep private what you see at work\n• Able to clear background verification\n• Housekeeping experience is preferred",
    benefits: "What we offer\n• Paid leave: 12 casual leave and 6 sick leave days a year, plus compensatory off for eligible extra days worked\n• PF and ESI as applicable\n\nBefore you join\n• Your offer is subject to background and reference verification and a police clearance certificate",
    hr_notes: "Standard terms\n• No standard CTC is recorded for this designation yet; agree the figure with management before publishing pay\n• Police clearance certificate and background verification are compulsory before joining\n\nWhat to test in the interview\n• Desk rule: point to a desk with papers and a phone on it and ask how they would clean it. The right answer is to clean only the clear part and move nothing\n• Found items: ask what they would do with a key card or a sheet of paper found on the floor. The right answer is to pick it up and hand it to the HR Manager without reading it\n• Printer paper: ask what they would do with printouts left by the printer at the end of the day. The right answer is to leave them; staff put paper for disposal in the shred bin\n• Reading Hindi: ask them to read a line from a cleaning schedule and a safety label aloud\n• Visitors: ask what they would do if a stranger asks to be let into the office. The right answer is to send the person to the Security Guard or reception\n\nSource: JD Compendium v4.2, BVT/HR/JD/2026/039",
